From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: vote zero bandwidth before GMU slumber

On the way into system suspend devfreq calls a6xx_gmu_set_freq() with
suspended=true, which records the frequency and returns before sending
the HFI GX_BW_PERF_VOTE. a6xx_gmu_shutdown() then asks the GMU to
slumber with whatever bandwidth level was last active still voted on the
GMU's RSC DRV. On the AYN Odin 3 (SM8750, Adreno 830, GMU fw 5.1.25)
the AOP's DDR low-power-mode monitor shows the GPU DRV holding a DDR
vote for the whole of s2idle while every other master is at zero, so
DDR stays at 1555 MHz, CX never power-collapses and the device drains
about 1.9 %/h asleep. kgsl passes explicit levels to the GMU on the way
to slumber; mainline passes nothing.

Send an explicit vote for perf level 0 and bandwidth level 0 (the
all-zero BCM commands) before prepare-slumber. a6xx_gmu_resume() already
resets gmu->freq and re-votes the current OPP on the way back up.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1433,6 +1433,20 @@
 	/* If the GMU isn't responding assume it is hung */
 	if (ret)
 		goto force_off;
+
+	/*
+	 * Drop the GMU's DDR bandwidth vote before slumber. On the way down
+	 * devfreq calls a6xx_gmu_set_freq() with suspended=true, which only
+	 * records the frequency and never sends the HFI vote, so the GMU's
+	 * RSC DRV keeps whatever bandwidth level was last active. The AOP
+	 * then sees the GPU still requiring DDR through system suspend and
+	 * never collapses DDR or CX (observed on SM8750/A830 with the AOP's
+	 * DDR low-power-mode monitor). Vote the lowest perf level and the
+	 * zero bandwidth level explicitly; a6xx_gmu_resume() re-votes the
+	 * real OPP on the way back up.
+	 */
+	if (!gmu->legacy)
+		a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, 0, 0);
 
 	adreno_gpu->funcs->bus_halt(adreno_gpu, a6xx_gpu->hung);
 
